# Listening-Analytics API

A personal music analytics API that ingests data from Last.fm, built as a learning lab for backend architecture, REST, GraphQL, database design, and software architecture.

[![Run in Postman](https://run.pstmn.io/button.svg)](https://god.postman.co/run-collection/listening-analytics)

---

## 🎯 Architecture & Learning Strategy

This project is structured around **evolutionary architecture** and progressive cognitive learning:

```txt
V1: REST API (Express, Prisma, SQLite)
  ↓
V2: GraphQL API (Apollo Server, Express Integration)
  ↓
V3: Serverless / Cloud Functions
```

The domain model, business rules, and analytical queries remain constant while the delivery mechanism changes.

### 🧠 Software Design vs. System Design Strategy

* **Phases V1 to V3 (Software Architecture & Software Design):** Primary focus on code design within application boundaries — layered architecture (`Controller`, `Service`, `Repository`), clean domain abstractions, Prisma/SQL queries, and comparing developer experience (DX) between REST and GraphQL.
* **Phase V3+ (System Design & Distributed Systems):** Gradual transition to infra/system design topics — rate-limiting external API ingestion, background processing queues for Last.fm sync, caching layers with Redis, and cloud deployment topology.

